<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shallum of Israel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 752 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century-bce">8th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shallum was king of Israel for one month around 752 BCE, according to the Bible. He seized the throne by murdering Zechariah, the last king of the dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jehu">Jehu</a>, and was himself killed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menahem">Menahem</a>. His brief reign was one of a series of violent successions that weakened the northern kingdom in its last decades before the Assyrian conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shallum-of-israel.jpg" alt="Shallum of Israel" width="160" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michel Wolgemut, Wilhelm Pleydenwurff · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nuremberg_chronicles_f_53v_3.(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After the death of Jeroboam II the throne changed hands repeatedly by murder: Zechariah, <b>Shallum</b>, Menahem, Pekahiah and Pekah all reigned within about fifteen years.</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-israel">Kingdom of Israel · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Died in Samaria, in what is now <a href="/countries/palestine">Palestine</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=32.28,35.2&amp;year=-752" aria-label="Samaria on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5455 990 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Shallum of Israel"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5905 1260h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5905 1260h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=32.28,35.2&amp;year=-752">What was here in 752 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
